:: Define Schedule [system] {"position":"500,0","size":"100,100"}
/* Routines and daily plans ====================================================
   Where mom and sister are, and what they do, works in two layers:

   1. A ROUTINE (setup.routines.<sysName>.<routineId>, constants below) says what MAY happen in each
      of the 21 action rows of a day (row = time slot * 3 + action, see $timeSlots).
   2. The PLAN ($mom.plan / $sister.plan, story variables) is what WILL happen today. It is rolled from
      the routine once per day (Daily Update, or the first time anyone asks for it that day), so it
      stays the same for the whole day, even after a reload.

   Scheduled tasks ($activeTasks) are not written into either of them. They are laid on top when
   someone asks where she is (setup.npcAt / setup.npcNow), so a task that does not run (weekend, not
   enough energy, missed) simply leaves her in her plan.

   Which routine she follows lives in the state, by name only:
       $mom.routine = { weekday: "mom_stage0", weekend: "weekend" }
   A single weekday (0 Mon ... 6 Sun) can get its own routine: { weekday: "...", weekend: "...", 4: "friday_out" }.
   Story code switches routines with  <<run setup.useRoutine("mom", "weekday", "mom_stage1")>>

   A routine ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   {
       extends: "mom_stage0",   optional: start from that routine (of the same character) and change only
                           what this one names. rows is then an OBJECT of the rows that differ, keyed by
                           row number: { 12: [ ...options ], 13: [ ...options ] } (a full array replaces all
                           21). tasks and extras come from the base unless this routine has its own.
                           A base can extend another routine too
       rows: [ 21 rows ],  each row is an ARRAY OF OPTIONS, one of them is picked:
           { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ], weight: 2, requirements: [ "..." ] }
               location      sysName of the place (Define Locations)
               activity      activity ids (Define Activities), one of them is picked.
                             Empty or left out: a random activity of hers for that place whose "when"
                             includes the time slot (activities without "when" are never picked that way)
               weight        optional, how likely this option is compared to the others (default 1)
               requirements  optional TwineScript strings, all must be true or the option is dropped
           One option with one activity is a PINNED row: it always happens and extras never replace it.
           Pin everything the story relies on (sleep, meals, work).
       tasks: [ { first: 4, last: 11 [, requirements: [ "..." ]] } ],
                           rows (both ends included) the CMD scheduler may put tasks into. All other rows
                           are locked there. Tasks only run on weekdays, so weekend rows are always locked
       extras: [ { location: "bathroom", activity: [ "peeing" ], times: [0, 2], from: [ "home" ] }, ... ],
                           short visits sprinkled over the day, min to max times. Always only into rows that
                           are not pinned, not covered by a task today, and never next to another extra or to
                           a row that is already at that place. Each extra narrows it down further with:
               when          optional time slots it may happen in (default any)
               from          optional places she has to be planned at for the row to be replaced: sysNames
                             or group names from setup.locationGroups ("home"). Default: anywhere
               requirements  optional TwineScript strings, checked once when the day is planned
               check         optional function (cell, row, who) returning true if this row may be
                             replaced. cell is the planned { location, activity }. For anything the fields
                             above can not express, e.g. check: (cell) => cell.activity !== "studying"
   }

   Activities can carry two more fields for the plan (Define Activities):
       when:     [ 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 ]   time slots in which a random pick may choose it
       duration: [ 2, 3 ]            once picked, it goes on for that many actions (random between the two)
                                     as long as the following rows allow it. Default 1

   setup.privateLocations: places only one of them uses at a time (the bathroom). An option or extra
   there is skipped while the other one is already planned there, unless it is the only choice.
   setup.locationGroups: names for several places at once, usable in the "from" of an extra.
   setup.inLocations(place, list)  is the place (sysName) one of list (sysNames or group names)?

   Helpers:
   setup.useRoutine(who, day, id)       switch routine: day = "weekday", "weekend" or 0-6 (id null removes
                                        a single-day routine). Replans the rest of today if today changed
   setup.getRoutineId(who [, weekday])  the routine id for that weekday (default today)
   setup.getRoutine(who [, weekday])    the routine itself, with "extends" applied
   setup.resolveRoutine(who, id)        any routine by id, with "extends" applied (undefined and a console
                                        error if it does not exist)
   setup.checkRoutines()                console errors for every broken routine (wrong row count, a row
                                        without options, unknown place or activity). Runs at the end of
                                        this passage, so a mistake shows up as soon as the game starts
   setup.isTaskRow(who, row [, weekday])  may the CMD scheduler put a task in this row?
   setup.planDay([who [, fromRow]])     rolls today's plan (both when who is left out). Rows before
                                        fromRow keep what they had
   setup.getPlan(who)                   today's plan { day, routine, rows: [ { location, activity [, extra] } ] },
                                        rolled first if it is from another day
   setup.npcAt(who, row)                { location, activity, task, extra } at that row today: the running
                                        task (current row) or the scheduled one (other rows), else the plan.
                                        location is the $locations entry, task the $activeTasks entry
   setup.npcNow(who)                    the same for the current row
   setup.npcIsAt(who, place)            is she at that place (sysName) right now? For event requirements
   setup.updateNpcPositions()           PassageReady: copies npcNow into $mom/$sister.location and .activity
   setup.describePlan(who)              the plan for the profile: per time slot, merged cells
   (who = "mom", "sister" or the NPC object)
*/
<<set setup.routines to {
    mom: {
        /* Stage 0, until False Sympathy: she still works at the office of her boss */
        mom_stage0: {
            rows: [
                /* Early Morning */
                [ { location: "momroom", activity: [ "sleeping" ] } ],
                [ { location: "momroom", activity: [ "sleeping", "getting_dressed" ] } ],
                [ { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "cooking" ] } ],
                /* Morning */
                [ { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "cooking" ] } ], /* Breakfast */
                [ { location: "bathroom", activity: [ "showering" ] }, { location: "momroom", activity: [ "getting_dressed" ] } ],
                [ { location: "momswork", activity: [ "working_boss" ] } ],
                /* Noon */
                [ { location: "momswork", activity: [ "working_boss" ] } ],
                [ { location: "momswork", activity: [ "working_boss" ] } ],
                [ { location: "momswork", activity: [ "working_boss" ] } ],
                /* Afternoon */
                [ { location: "momswork", activity: [ "working_boss" ] } ],
                [ { location: "momswork", activity: [ "working_boss" ] } ],
                [ { location: "momswork", activity: [ "working_boss" ] } ],
                /* Evening */
                [ { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "cooking" ] } ], /* Dinner */
                [ { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "cleaning_kitchen" ] } ],
                [ { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "cleaning_kitchen" ] }, { location: "momroom" } ],
                /* Night */
                [ { location: "momroom", weight: 2 }, { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ] } ],
                [ { location: "momroom", weight: 2 }, { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ] } ],
                [ { location: "momroom" } ],
                /* Late Night */
                [ { location: "momroom", activity: [ "sleeping" ] } ],
                [ { location: "momroom", activity: [ "sleeping" ] } ],
                [ { location: "momroom", activity: [ "sleeping" ] } ],
            ],
            tasks: [ { first: 4, last: 11 } ],
            extras: [
                { location: "bathroom", activity: [ "peeing" ], times: [0, 2], from: [ "home" ] },
                { location: "bathroom", activity: [ "showering" ], times: [0, 1], when: [4, 5], from: [ "home" ] },
            ],
        },
        /* Stage 0, after False Sympathy: fired, home all day. Like mom_stage0, but her work hours are free time */
        stage0_fired: {
            extends: "mom_stage0",
            rows: {
                /* Morning 3 */
                5: [ { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "cleaning_kitchen" ] }, { location: "momroom" } ],
                /* Noon */
                6: [ { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "cleaning_kitchen" ] }, { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "momroom" } ],
                7: [ { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "cooking" ] } ],
                8: [ { location: "momroom", weight: 2 }, { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ] } ],
                /* Afternoon */
                9: [ { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "cleaning_kitchen" ] }, { location: "momroom" } ],
                10: [ { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "cleaning_kitchen" ] }, { location: "momroom" } ],
                11: [ { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "cleaning_kitchen" ] }, { location: "momroom" } ],
            },
        },
        /* Stage 1 (Stage 1 Follow Up): she works at my office. Like mom_stage0, but at my office from Morning 2 on */
        mom_stage1: {
            extends: "mom_stage0",
            rows: {
                /* Morning 2 and 3 */
                4: [ { location: "companystage1", activity: [ "working" ] } ],
                5: [ { location: "companystage1", activity: [ "working" ] } ],
                /* Noon */
                6: [ { location: "companystage1", activity: [ "working" ] } ],
                7: [ { location: "companystage1", activity: [ "working" ] } ],
                8: [ { location: "companystage1", activity: [ "working" ] } ],
                /* Afternoon */
                9: [ { location: "companystage1", activity: [ "working" ] } ],
                10: [ { location: "companystage1", activity: [ "working" ] } ],
                11: [ { location: "companystage1", activity: [ "working" ] } ],
            },
            tasks: [
                { first: 4, last: 11 },
                /* the evening opens up after How is your new job? */
                { first: 12, last: 14, requirements: [ "setup.questDone('mom_newJobImpression')" ] },
                /* the night, for the Client Evening with her daughter (Define Tasks) */
                { first: 15, last: 17, requirements: [ "setup.taskUnlocked('task_mom_client_evening')" ] },
            ],
        },
        /* Saturday and Sunday, every stage */
        weekend: {
            rows: [
                /* Early Morning */
                [ { location: "momroom", activity: [ "sleeping" ] } ],
                [ { location: "momroom", activity: [ "sleeping" ] } ],
                [ { location: "momroom", activity: [ "sleeping", "getting_dressed" ] }, { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "cooking" ] } ],
                /* Morning: breakfast */
                [ { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "cooking" ] } ],
                [ { location: "bathroom", activity: [ "showering" ] }, { location: "momroom", activity: [ "getting_dressed" ] }, { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ] } ],
                [ { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "cleaning_kitchen" ] }, { location: "momroom" } ],
                /* Noon */
                [ { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "cleaning_kitchen" ] }, { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ] }, { location: "momroom" } ],
                [ { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "cooking" ] } ],
                [ { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "cooking" ] } ],
                /* Afternoon: lunch */
                [ { location: "momroom", weight: 2 }, { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ] } ],
                [ { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "cleaning_kitchen" ] }, { location: "momroom" } ],
                [ { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "cleaning_kitchen" ] }, { location: "momroom" } ],
                /* Evening: dinner */
                [ { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "cooking" ] } ],
                [ { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "cleaning_kitchen" ] } ],
                [ { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "cleaning_kitchen" ] }, { location: "momroom" } ],
                /* Night */
                [ { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "momroom" } ],
                [ { location: "momroom", weight: 2 }, { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ] } ],
                [ { location: "momroom" } ],
                /* Late Night */
                [ { location: "momroom", activity: [ "sleeping" ] } ],
                [ { location: "momroom", activity: [ "sleeping" ] } ],
                [ { location: "momroom", activity: [ "sleeping" ] } ],
            ],
            tasks: [],
            extras: [
                { location: "bathroom", activity: [ "peeing" ], times: [0, 2], from: [ "home" ] },
                { location: "bathroom", activity: [ "showering" ], times: [0, 1], when: [1, 4, 5], from: [ "home" ] },
            ],
        },
    },
    /*
    ==========================================================================================================
    ===============================================   Sister   ===============================================
    ==========================================================================================================
    */
    sister: {
        /* Stage 0: classes in the morning, free afternoon (chores once More Time Needed is done) */
        sister_stage0: {
            rows: [
                /* Early Morning */
                [ { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "sleeping" ] } ],
                [ { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "sleeping" ] } ],
                [ { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "sleeping", "watching_reels" ] } ],
                /* Morning: breakfast */
                [ { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "doing_chores" ] } ],
                [ { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "watching_reels" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "bathroom", activity: [ "showering" ] } ],
                [ { location: "college", activity: [ "studying_college" ] } ],
                /* Noon */
                [ { location: "college", activity: [ "studying_college" ] } ],
                [ { location: "college", activity: [ "studying_college" ] } ],
                [ { location: "college", activity: [ "studying_college" ] } ],
                /* Afternoon */
                [
                    { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "doing_chores" ], requirements: [ "$sister.flags.doesChores" ] },
                    { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ], weight: 2, requirements: [ "!$sister.flags.doesChores" ] },
                    { location: "sisterroom", requirements: [ "!$sister.flags.doesChores" ] },
                ],
                [
                    { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "doing_chores" ], requirements: [ "$sister.flags.doesChores" ] },
                    { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ], weight: 2, requirements: [ "!$sister.flags.doesChores" ] },
                    { location: "sisterroom", requirements: [ "!$sister.flags.doesChores" ] },
                ],
                [ { location: "sisterroom", weight: 2 }, { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ] } ],
                /* Evening: dinner */
                [ { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "doing_chores" ] } ],
                [ { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "studying" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "watching_reels" ] }, { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ] } ],
                [ { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "studying" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "watching_reels" ] }, { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ] } ],
                /* Night */
                [ { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "watching_reels" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ] } ],
                [ { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ] }, { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "watching_reels" ] } ],
                [ { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ] }, { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "watching_reels" ] } ],
                /* Late Night */
                [ { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "sleeping" ] } ],
                [ { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "sleeping" ] } ],
                [ { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "sleeping" ] } ],
            ],
            extras: [
                { location: "bathroom", activity: [ "peeing" ], times: [0, 2], from: [ "home" ] },
                { location: "bathroom", activity: [ "showering" ], times: [0, 1], when: [4, 5], from: [ "home" ] },
            ],
        },
        /* Stage 1 (Stage 1 Follow Up): like sister_stage0, but her afternoons are at my office */
        sister_stage1: {
            extends: "sister_stage0",
            rows: {
                /* Afternoon */
                9: [ { location: "companystage1", activity: [ "working" ] } ],
                10: [ { location: "companystage1", activity: [ "working" ] } ],
                11: [ { location: "companystage1", activity: [ "working" ] } ],
            },
            tasks: [ 
                { first: 9, last: 11 },
                { first: 6, last: 8, requirements: [ "setup.questDone('sister_mostlyDone')" ] },
                /* the evening opens up after What Are We: she starts staying late, to be near me (Overtime) */
                { first: 12, last: 14, requirements: [ "setup.questDone('sister_whatAreWe')" ] },
                /* the night, for the Client Evening with her mother (Define Tasks) */
                { first: 15, last: 17, requirements: [ "setup.taskUnlocked('task_sister_client_evening')" ] },
            ],
        },
        sister_stage1_noon: {
            extends: "sister_stage1",
            rows: {
                /* Afternoon */
                6: [ { location: "companystage1", activity: [ "working" ] } ],
                7: [ { location: "companystage1", activity: [ "working" ] } ],
                8: [ { location: "companystage1", activity: [ "working" ] } ],
            },
        },
        /* Saturday and Sunday, every stage */
        weekend: {
            rows: [
                /* Early Morning */
                [ { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "sleeping" ] } ],
                [ { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "sleeping" ] } ],
                [ { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "sleeping" ] } ],
                /* Morning: breakfast */
                [ { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "doing_chores" ] } ],
                [ { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "watching_reels" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "bathroom", activity: [ "showering" ] } ],
                [ { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "watching_reels" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ] } ],
                /* Noon */
                [ { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "doing_chores" ] } ],
                [ { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "studying", "watching_reels" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ] } ],
                [ { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "studying", "watching_reels" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ] } ],
                /* Afternoon: lunch */
                [ { location: "sisterroom", weight: 2 }, { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ] } ],
                [ { location: "sisterroom", weight: 2 }, { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ] } ],
                [ { location: "sisterroom", weight: 2 }, { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ] } ],
                /* Evening: dinner */
                [ { location: "kitchen", activity: [ "doing_chores" ] } ],
                [ { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "watching_reels" ] } ],
                [ { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "watching_reels" ] } ],
                /* Night */
                [ { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "watching_reels" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ] } ],
                [ { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "watching_reels" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ] } ],
                [ { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "watching_reels" ], weight: 2 }, { location: "livingroom", activity: [ "watching_tv" ] } ],
                /* Late Night */
                [ { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "sleeping" ] } ],
                [ { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "sleeping" ] } ],
                [ { location: "sisterroom", activity: [ "sleeping" ] } ],
            ],
            tasks: [],
            extras: [
                { location: "bathroom", activity: [ "peeing" ], times: [0, 2], from: [ "home" ] },
                { location: "bathroom", activity: [ "showering" ], times: [0, 1], when: [4, 5], from: [ "home" ] },
            ],
        },
    },
}>>

<<set setup.scheduleNpcs to ["mom", "sister"]>>
<<set setup.privateLocations to ["bathroom"]>>
<<set setup.locationGroups to {
    home: [ "hallway", "bedroom", "livingroom", "kitchen", "bathroom", "momroom", "sisterroom" ],
}>>

/* The routine each of them starts with. Plans are rolled on demand (setup.getPlan) */
<<set $mom.routine to { weekday: "mom_stage0", weekend: "weekend" }>>
<<set $mom.plan to null>>
<<set $sister.routine to { weekday: "sister_stage0", weekend: "weekend" }>>
<<set $sister.plan to null>>

/* Small helpers ============================================================== */
<<set setup.scheduleKey = (who) => {
    return (who && typeof who === "object") ? who.sysName : who;
}>>

<<set setup.scheduleRowCount = () => {
    return State.variables.timeSlots.length * State.variables.time.actions.max;
}>>

<<set setup.scheduleCurrentRow = () => {
    const t = State.variables.time;
    return t.current.value * t.actions.max + (t.actions.max - t.actions.left);
}>>

<<set setup.scheduleRequirementsMet = (list) => {
    return (list || []).every((req) => {
        try {
            return !!Scripting.evalTwineScript(req);
        } catch (e) {
            console.error('Schedule requirement "' + req + '" failed: ' + e.message);
            return false;
        }
    });
}>>

<<set setup.scheduleLocationOpen = (place, slot) => {
    const loc = setup.getLocationBySysName(place);
    return !!loc && (!Array.isArray(loc.open) || loc.open.length === 0 || loc.open.includes(slot));
}>>

<<set setup.inLocations = (place, list) => {
    return (list || []).some((entry) => entry === place
        || (Array.isArray(setup.locationGroups[entry]) && setup.locationGroups[entry].includes(place)));
}>>

<<set setup.randomInt = (min, max) => {
    return min + Math.floor(Math.random() * (max - min + 1));
}>>

<<set setup.pickWeighted = (list, weightOf) => {
    if (!list.length) { return undefined; }
    const total = list.reduce((sum, item) => sum + weightOf(item), 0);
    let roll = Math.random() * total;
    for (const item of list) {
        roll -= weightOf(item);
        if (roll < 0) { return item; }
    }
    return list[list.length - 1];
}>>

/* Routines ==================================================================== */

<<set setup.getRoutineId = (who, weekday) => {
    const v = State.variables;
    const npc = v[setup.scheduleKey(who)];
    const day = (weekday == null) ? v.date.today.value : weekday;
    return npc.routine[day] || npc.routine[day < 5 ? "weekday" : "weekend"];
}>>

<<set setup.resolveRoutine = (who, id, chain) => {
    const key = setup.scheduleKey(who);
    const own = (setup.routines[key] || {})[id];
    if (!own) {
        console.error('setup.resolveRoutine: "' + key + '" has no routine "' + id + '"');
        return undefined;
    }
    if (!own.extends) { return own; }

    const seen = (chain || []).concat(id);
    if (seen.includes(own.extends)) {
        console.error('setup.resolveRoutine: routines of "' + key + '" extend each other in a circle: ' + seen.concat(own.extends).join(" > "));
        return undefined;
    }
    const base = setup.resolveRoutine(key, own.extends, seen);
    if (!base) { return undefined; }

    let rows = (base.rows || []).slice();
    if (Array.isArray(own.rows)) {
        rows = own.rows;
    } else if (own.rows) {
        Object.keys(own.rows).forEach((row) => {
            const index = Number(row);
            if (!(index >= 0 && index < rows.length)) {
                console.error('setup.resolveRoutine: routine "' + id + '" of "' + key + '" changes row ' + row + ', which does not exist');
                return;
            }
            rows[index] = own.rows[row];
        });
    }
    return {
        rows: rows,
        tasks: own.tasks || base.tasks || [],
        extras: own.extras || base.extras || [],
    };
}>>

<<set setup.getRoutine = (who, weekday) => {
    const key = setup.scheduleKey(who);
    return setup.resolveRoutine(key, setup.getRoutineId(key, weekday));
}>>

<<set setup.checkRoutines = () => {
    const total = setup.scheduleRowCount();
    Object.keys(setup.routines).forEach((key) => {
        Object.keys(setup.routines[key]).forEach((id) => {
            const routine = setup.resolveRoutine(key, id);
            if (!routine) { return; }
            const where = 'Routine "' + id + '" of "' + key + '"';
            if (routine.rows.length !== total) {
                console.error(where + " has " + routine.rows.length + " rows instead of " + total);
            }
            const entries = [];
            routine.rows.forEach((row, index) => {
                const list = Array.isArray(row) ? row : (row ? [row] : []);
                if (!list.length) { console.error(where + ": row " + index + " has no options"); }
                list.forEach((option) => entries.push({ option: option, at: "row " + index }));
            });
            (routine.extras || []).forEach((extra, index) => entries.push({ option: extra, at: "extra " + index }));
            entries.forEach((entry) => {
                if (!setup.getLocationBySysName(entry.option.location)) {
                    console.error(where + ", " + entry.at + ': unknown place "' + entry.option.location + '"');
                }
                [].concat(entry.option.activity || []).forEach((activity) => {
                    if (!(setup.activities[key] || {})[activity]) {
                        console.error(where + ", " + entry.at + ': unknown activity "' + activity + '"');
                    }
                });
            });
        });
    });
}>>

<<set setup.useRoutine = (who, day, id) => {
    const v = State.variables;
    const key = setup.scheduleKey(who);
    if (id != null && !(setup.routines[key] || {})[id]) {
        console.error('setup.useRoutine: "' + key + '" has no routine "' + id + '"');
        return;
    }
    const before = setup.getRoutineId(key);
    if (id == null) {
        delete v[key].routine[day];
    } else {
        v[key].routine[day] = id;
    }
    const plan = v[key].plan;
    if (plan && plan.day === v.date.dayCount && setup.getRoutineId(key) !== before) {
        setup.planDay(key, setup.scheduleCurrentRow());
    }
}>>

<<set setup.isTaskRow = (who, row, weekday) => {
    const v = State.variables;
    const day = (weekday == null) ? v.date.today.value : weekday;
    /* tasks only run on weekdays (checkTaskProgression) */
    if (day >= 5) { return false; }
    const routine = setup.getRoutine(who, day);
    return !!routine && (routine.tasks || []).some((range) =>
        row >= range.first && row <= range.last && setup.scheduleRequirementsMet(range.requirements));
}>>

/* The options of one routine row that pass their requirements, with activity as an array and a weight */
<<set setup.routineOptions = (who, routine, row) => {
    const raw = (routine && routine.rows) ? routine.rows[row] : undefined;
    const list = Array.isArray(raw) ? raw : (raw ? [raw] : []);
    return list
        .filter((option) => setup.scheduleRequirementsMet(option.requirements))
        .map((option) => ({
            location: option.location,
            activity: [].concat(option.activity || []),
            weight: (Number(option.weight) > 0) ? Number(option.weight) : 1,
        }));
}>>

/* Activity ids an option can pick from: its own list, or the random pool of the place */
<<set setup.optionActivities = (who, option, slot) => {
    if (option.activity.length) { return option.activity; }
    const loc = setup.getLocationBySysName(option.location);
    if (!loc) { return []; }
    return setup.getActivitiesForLocation(who, loc)
        .filter((activity) => Array.isArray(activity.when) && activity.when.includes(slot))
        .map((activity) => activity.id);
}>>

/* Plans ======================================================================= */

/* Rolls the 21 rows of one day. others = plans of the other NPCs for the same day (private places) */
<<set setup.buildPlan = (who, weekday, others) => {
    const v = State.variables;
    const key = setup.scheduleKey(who);
    const routine = setup.getRoutine(key, weekday);
    const max = v.time.actions.max;
    const total = setup.scheduleRowCount();
    const takenAt = (row, place) => setup.privateLocations.includes(place)
        && others.some((plan) => plan.rows[row] && plan.rows[row].location === place);
    const rows = [];
    const flexible = [];
    let current = null;

    for (let row = 0; row < total; row++) {
        const slot = Math.floor(row / max);
        const all = setup.routineOptions(key, routine, row);
        flexible.push(all.length > 1 || (all.length === 1 && all[0].activity.length !== 1));

        let options = all.filter((option) => setup.scheduleLocationOpen(option.location, slot));
        if (!options.length) { options = all; }
        const free = options.filter((option) => !takenAt(row, option.location));
        if (free.length) { options = free; }

        if (!options.length) {
            console.error('setup.buildPlan: row ' + row + ' of the routine "' + setup.getRoutineId(key, weekday) + '" of ' + key + ' has no option');
            rows.push(rows.length ? clone(rows[rows.length - 1]) : { location: "hallway", activity: "" });
            current = null;
            continue;
        }

        /* keep doing the same thing while its duration lasts and this row allows it */
        if (current && current.left > 0 && options.some((option) => option.location === current.location
                && setup.optionActivities(key, option, slot).includes(current.activity))) {
            current.left--;
            rows.push({ location: current.location, activity: current.activity });
            continue;
        }

        const option = setup.pickWeighted(options, (o) => o.weight);
        const ids = setup.optionActivities(key, option, slot);
        const activity = ids.length ? ids[Math.floor(Math.random() * ids.length)] : "";
        if (!activity) {
            console.error('setup.buildPlan: ' + key + ' has no activity with "when" for ' + option.location + ' in time slot ' + slot);
        }
        const definition = activity ? setup.getActivity(key, activity) : undefined;
        const span = (definition && Array.isArray(definition.duration) && definition.duration.length) ? definition.duration : [1, 1];
        current = { location: option.location, activity: activity, left: setup.randomInt(span[0], span[span.length - 1]) - 1 };
        rows.push({ location: option.location, activity: activity });
    }

    setup.placeScheduleExtras(key, routine, rows, flexible, weekday, others);
    return rows;
}>>

/* Sprinkles the routine extras (bathroom visits, ...) over the rows that are not pinned */
<<set setup.placeScheduleExtras = (who, routine, rows, flexible, weekday, others) => {
    const v = State.variables;
    const key = setup.scheduleKey(who);
    const max = v.time.actions.max;
    /* a task that rests today (cooldown, Define Tasks) leaves its rows to the routine */
    const tasks = (weekday < 5) ? ((v.activeTasks || {})[key] || []).filter((e) => !setup.taskRestsToday(e.task)) : [];
    const used = [];

    ((routine && routine.extras) || []).forEach((extra) => {
        if (!setup.scheduleRequirementsMet(extra.requirements)) { return; }
        const ids = [].concat(extra.activity || []);
        if (!ids.length) { return; }
        const times = extra.times || [1, 1];
        let count = setup.randomInt(times[0], times[times.length - 1]);

        const candidates = [];
        rows.forEach((cell, row) => {
            const slot = Math.floor(row / max);
            if (!flexible[row]) { return; }
            if (Array.isArray(extra.when) && !extra.when.includes(slot)) { return; }
            if (tasks.some((entry) => row >= entry.startRow && row < entry.endRow)) { return; }
            if ([rows[row - 1], rows[row + 1]].some((near) => near && near.location === extra.location)) { return; }
            if (Array.isArray(extra.from) && !setup.inLocations(cell.location, extra.from)) { return; }
            if (typeof extra.check === "function" && !extra.check(cell, row, key)) { return; }
            if (!setup.scheduleLocationOpen(extra.location, slot)) { return; }
            if (setup.privateLocations.includes(extra.location)
                && others.some((plan) => plan.rows[row] && plan.rows[row].location === extra.location)) { return; }
            candidates.push(row);
        });

        while (count > 0 && candidates.length) {
            const row = candidates.splice(Math.floor(Math.random() * candidates.length), 1)[0];
            if (used.some((other) => Math.abs(other - row) < 2)) { continue; }
            used.push(row);
            rows[row] = { location: extra.location, activity: ids[Math.floor(Math.random() * ids.length)], extra: true };
            count--;
        }
    });
}>>

<<set setup.planDay = (who, fromRow) => {
    const v = State.variables;
    const keys = who ? [setup.scheduleKey(who)] : setup.scheduleNpcs;
    keys.forEach((key) => {
        const npc = v[key];
        const others = setup.scheduleNpcs
            .filter((other) => other !== key && v[other].plan && v[other].plan.day === v.date.dayCount)
            .map((other) => v[other].plan);
        const rows = setup.buildPlan(key, v.date.today.value, others);
        const old = npc.plan;
        if (fromRow > 0 && old && old.day === v.date.dayCount) {
            for (let row = 0; row < fromRow && row < rows.length; row++) {
                rows[row] = old.rows[row];
            }
        }
        npc.plan = { day: v.date.dayCount, routine: setup.getRoutineId(key), rows: rows };
    });
}>>

<<set setup.getPlan = (who) => {
    const v = State.variables;
    const key = setup.scheduleKey(who);
    if (!v[key].plan || v[key].plan.day !== v.date.dayCount) {
        setup.planDay(key);
    }
    return v[key].plan;
}>>

/* Where is she, and what is she doing? =========================================
   Tasks only count on weekdays. In the current row only a task that really runs (inProgress) counts,
   in the other rows every scheduled one that was not missed today. */
<<set setup.npcAt = (who, row) => {
    const v = State.variables;
    const key = setup.scheduleKey(who);
    const now = (row === setup.scheduleCurrentRow());
    const entry = (v.date.today.value < 5)
        ? ((v.activeTasks || {})[key] || []).find((e) => row >= e.startRow && row < e.endRow
            && (now ? e.inProgress : (e.missedDay !== v.date.dayCount && !setup.taskRestsToday(e.task))))
        : undefined;
    const cell = setup.getPlan(key).rows[row] || {};
    const planned = setup.getLocationBySysName(cell.location);

    if (entry) {
        const task = setup.getLiveTask(entry.task);
        return {
            location: (task.location && v.locations[task.location.id]) || planned,
            activity: setup.getTaskActivity(task) || cell.activity,
            task: entry,
            extra: false,
        };
    }
    return { location: planned, activity: cell.activity, task: undefined, extra: !!cell.extra };
}>>

<<set setup.npcNow = (who) => {
    return setup.npcAt(who, setup.scheduleCurrentRow());
}>>

/* Is she at that place (sysName) right now? Reads npcNow, so it is right even before PassageReady has
   moved her (CheckForEvent runs first): use it in event requirements */
<<set setup.npcIsAt = (who, place) => {
    const now = setup.npcNow(who);
    return !!now.location && setup.sameLocation(now.location, setup.getLocationBySysName(place));
}>>

<<set setup.updateNpcPositions = () => {
    const v = State.variables;
    setup.scheduleNpcs.forEach((key) => {
        const npc = v[key];
        const now = setup.npcNow(key);
        if (!now.location) { return; }
        if (npc.location && npc.location.id !== now.location.id) {
            npc.previousLocation = clone(npc.location);
        }
        npc.location = clone(now.location);
        npc.activity = now.activity;
    });
}>>

/* The plan for the profile: one entry per time slot, neighbouring actions that are the same merged
   into one cell { place, doing, task, title, span, now, past } */
<<set setup.describePlan = (who) => {
    const v = State.variables;
    const key = setup.scheduleKey(who);
    const max = v.time.actions.max;
    const nowRow = setup.scheduleCurrentRow();
    return v.timeSlots.map((slot, s) => {
        const cells = [];
        for (let a = 0; a < max; a++) {
            const row = s * max + a;
            const at = setup.npcAt(key, row);
            const place = at.location ? wikifyText(at.location.name) : "";
            const doing = at.activity ? setup.activityText(key, at.activity) : "";
            const task = !!at.task;
            const last = cells[cells.length - 1];
            if (last && last.place === place && last.doing === doing && last.task === task) {
                last.span++;
                last.rows.push(row);
            } else {
                cells.push({
                    place: place,
                    doing: doing,
                    task: task,
                    title: task ? wikifyText(setup.getLiveTask(at.task.task).title) : "",
                    span: 1,
                    rows: [row],
                });
            }
        }
        cells.forEach((cell) => {
            cell.now = cell.rows.includes(nowRow);
            cell.past = cell.rows[cell.rows.length - 1] < nowRow;
        });
        return { text: slot.text, now: Math.floor(nowRow / max) === s, cells: cells };
    });
}>>

/* catches mistakes in the routines as soon as the game starts (see the browser console) */
<<run setup.checkRoutines()>>
